# RFC-254 T31 — line endings are part of this repository's contract, not a
# per-developer preference.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# --------------------
# Git for Windows installs default to `core.autocrlf=true`, and so does the
# `windows-latest` GitHub runner. Without this file, checking the repo out
# there rewrites every LF to CRLF, and that is not cosmetic:
#
#   * Source-lock tests match source text against regexes that spell `\n`
#     literally. Under CRLF the byte before the newline is `\r`, so the pattern
#     misses and the test reports a *product* defect ("clearSelection no longer
#     resets the dedupe sig") when nothing about the product changed. That is
#     precisely how the first Windows frontend leg went red — after the same
#     suite had been measured green on a real Windows host, where the tree had
#     arrived by tarball and kept its LF.
#   * All 4405 tracked files are LF today (verified: `git grep -Il $'\r'`
#     returns nothing), so declaring LF changes no content — it only stops the
#     checkout from changing it.
#
# The framework already pins `core.autocrlf=false` for the git operations it
# performs itself (`util/gitHardening.ts`), because CRLF rewriting reaches port
# values and model input. This file extends the same rule to the repository's
# own checkout, which that pin cannot cover.
#
# `eol=lf` is deliberate rather than `text=auto` alone: `auto` normalizes what
# goes INTO the object database but still honours the platform default coming
# out. Only `eol=lf` makes the working tree identical everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be touched. `text=auto` usually detects these, but
# the visual-regression baselines are compared byte-for-byte across three
# platforms — an accidental newline rewrite there would be reported as a UI
# change, so make the exclusion explicit rather than relying on detection.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.tgz binary
*.node binary
*.exe binary
